  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current algorithm uses gradient-based optimization and perturbation methods to reduce the maximum overlap integral. The approach addresses two main bottlenecks in this problem: the non-convex nature of the optimization landscape and the curse of dimensionality in high-resolution representations. The strategy improves upon the parent solution by implementing several key changes:\n\n- **Feature detection**: Introduces sparse representation where non-zero values represent characteristic features in the function.\n- **Multi-resolution optimization**: Balances between coarse and fine feature representations.\n- **Adaptive hyperparameter tuning**: Automatically adjusts optimization parameters based on progress and gradient behavior.\n- **Progressive refinement**: Uses shorter features first and gradually adds higher resolution.\n- **Geometric optimization**: Incorporates geometric constraints to preserve function properties.\n\nThe method reduces local optima by introducing structured randomness in feature positions, while maintaining global structure through optimization. This approach provides a better trade-off between exploration and exploitation without increasing computational complexity.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nThe optimization problem is defined on a step function h: [0,2] -> [0,1]:\n- **Function representation**: Piecewise constant function with n samples\n- **Constraints**: \n  - 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 \u2200x\n  - \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1\n- **Objective**: Minimize\n  max\u2096 \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx\n\nImplementation details:\n- Execution on paper\n- Helper functions: feature_placement, h_function, objective_function\n- Transformations between resolutions when parent is available\n- Validation via projection and normalization\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nSteps from input to output with dimension tracking and failure handling:\n\n**Parent validation**\nexp, dim = None, (the_parent = None)\nif parent_available:\n\tREQUIRE_PARENT_FORMAT()\n\tif not np.all((0 <= the_parent < MAX_VAL) & (FEATURE_BASE_LOGIC)):\n\t\t# Apply feature projection\n\t\ttransformed_parent = FEATURE_PROJECTION(parent_representation)\n\n**Resolution management**\nn_points = DEFAULT_RESOLUTION=300\nif parent_available:\n\tSAVE_ORIGINAL_RESOLUTION(n_points)\n\n**Optimization sequence**\n1. Feature selection (vectorized at intervals)\n2. Gradient-based expansion\n3. Progressive refinement (start coarse, end fine)\n4. Geometric enforcement (min-max)\n5. Boundary condition handling\n\n**Pseudocode for key operations**\ndef feature_placement(n): \n\treturn np.random.choice(FEATURE_POSSIBILITIES)\n\ndef objective_function(h): \n\tcompute_correlation(h, FULL_MODE)\n\treturn max_correlation * DX\n\ndef project_feasible(h, n):\n\tnorm = np.linalg.norm(h_sum_deviation)\n\tif norm < THRESHOLD: return h\n\treturn normalize_and_clip(h, n)\n\n**Numerically stable correlation handling**\nuse_vectorized_corr = False\ntry:\n  compute_full_correlation(h, method='full')\n  full_corr_value = np.min(correlation_output)  # approximated minimum overlap? \n  return full_corr_value * DX\nexcept MemoryError:\n  compute_approx_correlation(h)\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n**Default parameters and ranges**\nFEATURE_COUNT = 5-100\nOPTIMIZATION_STEPS = 10-100\nLEARNING_RATE_INITIAL = 0.01-0.1\nGEOMETRIC_TOLERANCE = 1e-5\n\n**Progressive adaptation**\n- If gradient becomes too small early: reduce FEATURE_COUNT threshold\n- If correlation decreases slowly: increase FEATURE_COUNT budget\n- Automatic feature position adjustment by gradient descent\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n**Time calculation**\n- Features per step: n_points/100\n- Each optimization step: 50-80% of time budget\n- Deadline checkpointing: monitor time at each resolution change\n\n**Fallback procedure**\ntry:\n  run_primary_optimization()\nexcept OptimizationFailure:\n  fallback_to_parent(n_points)\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFinal solution must:\n- Pass feasibility checks: zeros within bounds\n- Have integral \u2248 n/2 with tolerance 1e-4\n- Return (FEATURE_VECTOR, c5_bound, n_points)\n- Internal sanity checks:\n  assert(c5_bound is finite)\n  assert(h satisfies constraints)",
